# Reference only. Nexus never reads this file. Export a line in your shell before
# `./nexus run`, `./nexus rabbit ...` or `./doctor.sh`.
#
# The packaged service (`./nexus start`) receives only some of these. Which ones, and
# what to use instead, is in docs/service.md ("What the service receives").
#
# Older OS3_BRIDGE_* names: see docs/upgrading-from-os3-bridge.md.
#
# Provider keys. `./nexus run` reads these. The service reads the key files.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# NOUS_API_KEY=
#
# NEXUS_BACKEND=openrouter
#   Default only when .nexus_backend has not been saved. A Settings or setup choice
#   file wins over this, including after a packaged relaunch. Delete that file to make
#   this variable the backend again.
#   API keys: openrouter | openai | anthropic (alias claude) | xai (alias grok)
#   ChatGPT plan login over HTTP: chatgpt (alias chatgpt-plan). Works with OS3 tool calls.
#   OAuth: nous (Nous Portal, token copied from ~/.hermes/auth.json, refreshed by start)
#   Subscription CLIs, which refuse tool calls: codex | claude-code (alias claude-cli)
#     | copilot (alias github-copilot) | grok-build (alias grok-cli)
#     | antigravity (alias agy)
# NEXUS_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
#   Unset: each backend uses its own starting guess (docs/backends.md, Default models).
#   A starting guess is not an entitlement; set a model your account can use.
# NEXUS_MODEL_CHAT= / _WORKER= / _BACKGROUND= / _VISION=
#   Optional model per OS3 role; wins over the model OS3 sends. Unset: OS3's own.
#   Or put them in .nexus_roles.json (see CONNECT.md, Per-role models).
# NEXUS_MODEL_FALLBACK=off   # default on: serve the active model when OS3 names an id the backend's live list lacks (see CONNECT.md)
# NEXUS_FALLBACK=codex,claude-code,nous,openrouter
#   Optional ordered failover chain at a usage limit. Unset: off. See CONNECT.md.
# NEXUS_FALLBACK_COOLDOWN=900
# NEXUS_USAGE_SWITCH_PERCENT=95   # real used percent that benches the active backend early when a chain is set; off disables
#
# Subscription CLI paths, for a binary that is not on PATH.
# NEXUS_CODEX_BIN=
# NEXUS_CLAUDE_BIN=
# NEXUS_COPILOT_BIN=
# NEXUS_GROK_BIN=
# NEXUS_AGY_BIN=
# NEXUS_ENABLE_ANTIGRAVITY=1
#   Antigravity is off unless this is set (higher terms-of-service risk; see README, Provider risk).
#
# ChatGPT plan backend (chatgpt)
# NEXUS_CHATGPT_AUTH_FILE=   # Codex login file (default $CODEX_HOME/auth.json, else ~/.codex/auth.json)
# NEXUS_CHATGPT_CLIENT_VERSION=   # set if the model list is too short
# NEXUS_CHATGPT_USAGE_POLL=0   # default on: the dashboard reads plan usage from chatgpt.com at most once a minute
#
# Images
# NEXUS_IMAGES_BACKEND=chatgpt   # chatgpt | nous | off
# NEXUS_ENABLE_NOUS_IMAGES=1   # default off: Nous bills per image
# NEXUS_NOUS_IMAGE_DAILY_CAP=10
#
# Upstreams, timeouts and limits
# NEXUS_OPENAI_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
# NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_BASE=https://api.anthropic.com
# NEXUS_XAI_BASE=https://api.x.ai/v1
# NEXUS_STREAM_USAGE=0   # default on: ask OpenAI-style streams for token usage; 0 for a provider that rejects it
# NEXUS_MAX_INFLIGHT=8
# NEXUS_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT=120
# NEXUS_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=2   # seconds /health waits on a cold cache
# NEXUS_TOOL_REPAIR=off   # default on: repair malformed tool calls, or reject them as invalid_tool_call
#
# Address. Loopback only; any other host is refused.
# NEXUS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# NEXUS_PORT=11435
# NEXUS_SERVICE_LABEL=   # macOS LaunchAgent label for a second checkout (default ai.nexus.server)
#
# Install
# NEXUS_SKIP_UI=1   # install.sh: skip building the React dashboard
# NEXUS_UI_DIST=   # serve a built UI from this directory instead of ui/dist
#
# Rabbit OS3
# NEXUS_RABBIT_WATCHDOG=on   # default off (macOS): restart a crashed rabbit-agent LaunchAgent
# NEXUS_RABBIT_AGENT_LABEL=com.rabbit.rabbit-agent
# NEXUS_RABBIT_WATCHDOG_STATE=   # restart times for the 3/hour cap (default .nexus_rabbit_watchdog.json)
# NEXUS_RABBIT_SETUP=on   # default off: lets `./nexus rabbit setup|restore|verify` change Rabbit OS3 (undocumented web API)
# NEXUS_RABBIT_PROFILE=   # dedicated Chrome profile signed in to OS3 (see docs/rabbit-setup.md for the default)
# NEXUS_RABBIT_CDP_PORT=9333   # Chrome remote-debugging port, bound to 127.0.0.1 only
# NEXUS_RABBIT_CHROME_BIN=   # Chrome binary when it is not in the usual place
# NEXUS_RABBIT_BACKUP=   # saved previous OS3 connection, mode 600, no key (default .nexus_rabbit_backup.json)
# NEXUS_RABBIT_RESTORE_KEY_FILE=   # key file to put back a non-Nexus provider if setup fails
# NEXUS_RABBIT_KEY_DIRS=   # dirs (os.pathsep-separated) searched for that key file when the line above is unset
